<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The floor pin claim ~ a pin the place's KEL vouches for

A floor route takes its pin only through an authenticated relation or a carried signed pin set, and an
announcement never authenticates its own first pin (house ruling "The admit's gate pin"). A place's floor pin
derives from its floor key, which no seat holds, so no seat can mint it. The place claims it itself: this exact
pin, at one head of its own KEL, signed by the signer the KEL seats there. One relation carries the name
''floor pin claim'' (never "standing", which names realm standing, nor "position", which names causal coordinates).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-claim`>>

!! The claim ~ one per route per head

The place signs `{ kind, aid, seq, head, nexus, route, tier, digest }` (`PLACE_FLOOR_PIN_DOMAIN`, framed
`u32 len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage`; no sixth domain) with the signer its KEL seats at `head`. The Nexus AID anchors the
carrying relation and never signs as the place. The claim names NO release head: W26's release tracks floor
CONTENT, the claim tracks the place's KEY STATE, and nothing signs a release pointer into pin succession. It rides
the Nexus's carriage board under a sidecar key apart from the acts (`PLACE_FLOOR_PIN_PREFIX`, keyed by the AID, the
head and the pin's digest), beside the place's KEL rows (`place-kel-board`). Any replica writer may carry it; none can forge it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-reader`>>

!! The reader files only what it can vouch for

`readPlaceFloorPin` refuses by name, never throws, and files only when all of these hold:

# the claim reads whole and its pin reads whole (`readGateBundlePin`), at FLOOR tier, at the Nexus the reader asked, on the route asked;
# the reader's KEL rows fold to the named head (`foldClaimHead`: a walk from the head digest to the inception that is the AID, every digest, sequence, reveal and cold signature verified), on no forked branch (`head-unreadable`, `kel-forked`);
# the signer the KEL seats AT THAT HEAD signed this exact image (`verifyPlaceDutyAtHead`): an older signer after a rotation, and a forger, refuse `signature-refused`;
# LAST, the standing: the signer at the head is a counted `carry` of the reader's OWN held root (`place-uncarried`), or the AID is the anchor the reader was handed apart from the card (`place-unanchored`).

A card alone never anchors. Three conveyances stand: the founder's own genesis, an authenticated admit (a claim set a sovereign
crossing carried, whose first claim adopts the AID), and a deliberate person-to-person transfer (`#anchor=<aid>`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/descent`>>

!! KEL descent orders the pin

The pair index (`admit-gate-pin`) takes a claim with the lineage the reader folded (`fileClaim`) and folds its claims as a SET:
a descendant claim replaces; a known ancestor refuses `rollback` (and stays as ancestry evidence); two claims at one head, a
sibling rotation and another AID at one key surface as a fork and the index serves the settled ancestor, or nothing where none
is held; so no arrival order selects. A key rides its claims once a claim has filed: an unclaimed pin matches what is served or files
nothing. A rotated place serves under its new signer's name only, so the superseded key answers nothing. An offline reader holds its
last accepted head and says "as of my last sync" (`lastSyncNote`). Node and browser run this one fold. Floor-route keys derive from
the place floor key, tier, Nexus and route (`gate-bundle`), so a pin changes on its route only when the place key rotates: no
per-route successor log. The SOVEREIGN tier's pins follow custody-key changes by their own signed relation; a place-KEL claim never
orders them and the index refuses one by name (`claim-moves-no-sovereign-pin`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-carry`>>

!! The carry lands the claim

A carry crosses vaults as a PARTIAL with its claim and the KEL rows that fold to its head (`nexus-partial`, family `carry`). The claim
files ONLY with the counted act, in one write: a partial below the quorum exposes no pin. The judge reads the claim for the named
place at this Nexus, and the carrier seal verifies under the signer the KEL seats at the claim's head (`verifyCarrierContractAtHead`).
The herm carries the claim opaque. A rotated place is carried again under its new signer.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-place-arm`>>

!! The place arm

A place presents the quorum's counted `carry` act over its own key at the gate's Nexus, with every counted
act of that relation in its causal past as the lineage the gate's reader walks (`placeArmFor`,
`verifyPresentedCarry`). The head is the counted `carry` no other counted act of this place descends from; a
counted `uncarry` that descends from it leaves the place with no arm to present. A lineage past
`PLACE_LINEAGE_BOUND` presents nothing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/edges`>>

